       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervised care. Typical prescribing is lower:\n\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Anti-inflammatory use:** 400\u2013800 mg three to four times daily, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high risks GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It also adds little benefit, since ibuprofen's analgesic effect plateaus.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the ceiling, usually only for inflammatory conditions)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also review the order with your resident or attending. If you do want 1,600 mg per dose, the supervising prescriber will need to confirm that."
      }
     ],
